      <div class="msv__faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>How much does it cost to apply for the Non-Lucrative Visa in Spain?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Total costs depend on your nationality and whether you use professional support. For a single UK applicant without professional support, expect €1,500–€2,200 in visa-related costs (consulate fee, translations, apostille, medical, criminal record). Add €700–€1,200 for the first year of private health insurance. With My Spanish Visa professional support, the total investment is typically €2,500–€5,000 including the service fee, but this usually prevents costly rejections and delays.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What's included in the My Spanish Visa service fee for NLV applications?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>The My Spanish Visa service includes complete document checklist and management, professional translation coordination (translations included in service), document compilation and formatting for your consulate, consulate-specific requirements and guidance, application form support, consulate submission and appointment booking, post-arrival visa collection support, and dedicated client portal access. It does not include mandatory government fees (consulate fee, apostille processing, criminal record), health insurance, or flights.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How much do sworn Spanish translations cost for NLV documents?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Sworn translations in Spain typically cost €50–€150 per document. A typical NLV application requires 8–15 documents translated (criminal record, medical certificate, bank statements, educational documents, etc.), bringing translation costs to €400–€2,250. Longer or more complex documents cost more. When using My Spanish Visa, professional translations are coordinated and included in the service cost, which simplifies budgeting and often reduces per-document costs.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What hidden costs should I plan for with the Non-Lucrative Visa application?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Common "hidden" costs include apostille processing (£50–£200 per document from the UK, €10–€30 per document from the USA), bank letter fees (€10–€50 per letter, often needed 2–3 times), certified courier for documents (€30–€100 if sending originals by post), document notarization (€15–€30 per document), passport photos beyond consulate requirements (€10–€30), and potentially a passport renewal (£75 in the UK) if yours expires within 18 months. Budget an additional €300–€800 for these variable costs beyond the main items.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Is NLV renewal more expensive than the initial application?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>No. NLV renewal is significantly cheaper. You don't need to resubmit criminal record, medical certificate, education documents, or many other items. Renewal typically costs €800–€1,500 total, including the consulate fee (€80–€150), updated health insurance (€700–€1,200), and document fees. Initial applications cost €1,500–€3,500+ because of all the supporting documents needed. With My Spanish Visa renewal support, costs are typically €1,000–€1,500.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I reduce the cost of applying for the Non-Lucrative Visa?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Several strategies reduce costs: batch apostille requests to the UK Foreign Office (bulk rates are cheaper per document), use local Spanish sworn translators (often 30–50% cheaper than international agencies), ask your GP for the medical certificate rather than paying a private clinic €100–€150, obtain criminal records yourself rather than using intermediaries, plan health insurance purchases months in advance for better rates, and apply during low-season consulate periods. However, professional support from My Spanish Visa often saves more money overall by preventing rejections (€1,000+ cost) than it costs to hire.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What are the annual ongoing costs after my NLV is approved?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>After approval, annual costs typically include private health insurance (€700–€2,500 depending on age), income tax filing (€0–€500 if using online tools, or €200–€500 with a gestoría), and TIE card renewal every 10 years (€15–€30). Padrón registration is usually free. Optional costs include vehicle registration/insurance (€400–€1,000+ if you own a car), professional tax advisor (gestoría €200–€500/year), and NIE replacement (€15–€50 if lost). For most applicants, expect €800–€1,800 per year ongoing.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does the NLV cost vary if I'm applying from different consulates?</summary>
          <div class="msv__faq-answer">
            <p>Visa consulate fees (€80–€150) are the same across all Spanish consulates worldwide. However, total costs vary based on nationality and country of origin. UK applicants use the UK apostille process (£50–£200 per doc), USA applicants use the Secretary of State ($10–$30 per doc). Travel costs to reach the consulate also vary — a UK applicant may pay €200–€400 to travel to London, while an Australian applicant may pay €500–€1,500 to reach Madrid. Bottom line: the consulate fee is fixed, but total application cost depends on your home country more than the consulate location.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
